  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "Junctions in the native creation map",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Junctions in the native creation map (computed exactly on the seven small edge-atom trisum spaces: 29 to 47 points, three to five atoms, one junction each except one space with two). Yes/no creation alone reads the atoms: the lines no removal blocks are exactly the atom cores, and each root is created at by exactly six removals, its own core lines. With the atoms set aside it reads the junctions: a junction's two lines are never degenerate at the remaining removals and each is the only such removal that blocks the other, and no other pair of lines is, so the number of junctions is read too. Pair refinement of the native creation map makes same atom, square-mates and same leaf unions of stable pair classes, and the skeleton lines, junction lines, roots and loaded lines unions of diagonal classes; colour refinement of yes/no creation already separates the junction lines. Control: across REFINE-READ's 277 spaces a pair pinned apart from the atoms occurs once, in design 7, the only one whose glue holds a non-planar brace other than Heawood, at that brace's one trisector; no pair is pinned by yes/no creation alone. The spaces are HANDLE-COUNT A's generator's, each reproduced at its own seed under a recorded hash seed. These seven statements (P1 to P7) were frozen for ticket B's ten larger spaces before any of their maps was computed.",
